!!!A Lambda prenex
- Initially, {ce'u} was meant to be a PA, lambda-quantifying an otherwise logically-quantified variable (the {da}-series). Perhaps it is worth reviving this idea, although slightly modified, in an attempt to fix nested abstractions, which are otherwise messy, what with all the required subscripting. The original idea was for {ka} abstractions to be of the form ''lo ka ce'u da broda da'' for a reflexive property, and ''lo ka ce'u da broda ce'u de'' for non-reflexive properties.
